  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AACJ South Africa Alliance funds 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The G20 Presidency is hosted by South African in 2025. Oxfam South Africa is the host Oxfam country office, hence it has a vital role to play in amplifying climate change and climate justice considerations in the policy and decision-making processes of the G20. Through movement building, shifting narratives, innovative climate adaptation solutions and policy influencing OZA seeks to significantly shift the socio-economic and environmental wellbeing of people nationally, regionally and globally. OZA notesthat climate disasters, including natural disasters such as floods, droughts, wildfires, and occasional heatwaves, as well as socio-economic challenges that lead to humanitarian crises for marginalized people and communities have increased in frequency and intensity. Often, women and children are disproportionately affected by the adverse impacts of climate change. In response to these climate induced crises, OZA uses a Feminist Climate Justice lens, as it works with &#x201c;marginalized people and communities&#x201d;that are at the center of this climate crisis to mitigate the impact of these disasters and provide support to affected communities.</narrative>
  </description>
